# Applies to examples/docker/Dockerfile, whose build context is the monorepo
# root. BuildKit looks for <dockerfile>.dockerignore before the context-root
# .dockerignore, so this file is what takes effect. A .dockerignore sitting in
# this directory would be ignored entirely, because it is not at the context
# root.
**/node_modules
**/dist
# Without this, a host .tsbuildinfo makes `tsc -b` in the image think the
# (excluded) dist output is already up to date, and it emits nothing.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
.git
.claude
*.log
